WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.489 --> 00:00:13.869
swam hard through the waves.

2
00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:16.531
Because he was made of wood, he floated.

3
00:00:17.311 --> 00:00:19.232
But the waves threw him all around.

4
00:00:19.992 --> 00:00:21.773
Geppetto's boat was still far away.

5
00:00:21.793 --> 00:00:26.795
"I'll never reach Geppetto's boat in time!"

6
00:00:27.435 --> 00:00:28.256
Pinocchio cried.

7
00:00:29.204 --> 00:00:32.247
His mouth was full of salt water, and his arms were getting tired.

8
00:00:32.867 --> 00:00:33.708
But he kept swimming.

9
00:00:34.549 --> 00:00:36.830
To the side, he saw a small island.

10
00:00:37.571 --> 00:00:39.332
He swam to it so he could rest.

11
00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:45.458
While Pinocchio sat on the island, he looked for Geppetto's boat.

12
00:00:46.658 --> 00:00:48.580
"Oh, Father where are you?

13
00:00:49.381 --> 00:00:52.143
Wait, I see you!

14
00:00:52.443 --> 00:00:55.506
There is a whale by your boat and oh!

15
00:00:56.206 --> 00:00:57.968
The whale ate your boat!"

16
00:00:58.596 --> 00:01:00.557
Pinocchio could not see Geppetto anymore.

17
00:01:02.118 --> 00:01:03.478
He thought Geppetto had drowned.

18
00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:05.599
"Oh, Father!

19
00:01:06.119 --> 00:01:07.420
I didn't save you!

20
00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.561
I am so sorry.

21
00:01:09.581 --> 00:01:14.043
Whaaa!" Pinocchio cried.

22
00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:16.244
Just then, it started to rain.

23
00:01:16.264 --> 00:01:19.085
"Oh, I need to get dry.

24
00:01:19.605 --> 00:01:25.768
Father would want me to be safe and dry," Pinocchio said, and he ran into the nearby village.

25
00:01:28.108 --> 00:01:31.830
"Please, sir," he said to a man walking by with a coal cart.

26
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.951
"May I stay at your house, where it's dry?"

27
00:01:34.971 --> 00:01:41.474
"If you help me carry this coal, you may stay with me tonight," the man answered.

28
00:01:41.494 --> 00:01:45.255
"Oh, I don't want to carry coal!"

29
00:01:45.855 --> 00:01:47.056
Pinocchio said, offended.

30
00:01:47.856 --> 00:01:49.997
He wanted the man to help him without having to work.

31
00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:54.599
It rained harder.

32
00:01:54.619 --> 00:02:01.915
"Please, ma'am," he said to a woman carrying water jugs, "may I stay at your house where it's

33
00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:07.559
dry?" "If you help me carry these jugs, you may stay with me tonight."

34
00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:11.442
Pinocchio didn't want to carry the water jugs.

35
00:02:12.543 --> 00:02:14.904
But he wanted to be dry, so he agreed.

36
00:02:15.725 --> 00:02:18.827
The jugs were very heavy, but Pinocchio didn't complain.

37
00:02:19.587 --> 00:02:22.029
He carried them all the way to the woman's small house.

38
00:02:24.991 --> 00:02:26.512
Once inside, he sat down.

39
00:02:27.552 --> 00:02:28.613
"Here are the jugs.

40
00:02:29.173 --> 00:02:30.893
Thank you for letting me stay."

41
00:02:30.913 --> 00:02:34.075
"You are welcome," the woman said.

42
00:02:34.095 --> 00:02:37.276
"A little work never hurt anyone.

43
00:02:38.076 --> 00:02:39.197
Right, Pinocchio?"

44
00:02:39.217 --> 00:02:43.118
"How do you know my name?"

45
00:02:43.919 --> 00:02:45.079
he asked, surprised.

46
00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:50.001
The woman lifted her hood, and out fell her pretty blue hair.

47
00:02:50.021 --> 00:02:52.342
"Oh, Blue Fairy!

48
00:02:52.682 --> 00:02:53.263
It's you!

49
00:02:54.463 --> 00:02:56.324
But, why did you make me work?

50
00:02:56.796 --> 00:02:57.957
Why didn't you help me?"

51
00:02:58.437 --> 00:02:59.237
Pinocchio asked.

52
00:02:59.257 --> 00:03:01.838
"I did help you, Pinocchio.

53
00:03:03.019 --> 00:03:05.600
It is a good thing to get help from strangers.

54
00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:09.681
But it is an even better thing to help strangers.

55
00:03:11.042 --> 00:03:12.903
I wanted you to learn that lesson.

56
00:03:14.183 --> 00:03:16.604
Did you follow the road home as I showed you?"

57
00:03:17.184 --> 00:03:17.704
she asked.

58
00:03:17.724 --> 00:03:21.586
"I tried to follow the road," Pinocchio said.

59
00:03:21.606 --> 00:03:26.328
"But, I got trapped and then flown and then I swam.

60
00:03:27.144 --> 00:03:31.566
And when I stopped swimming, I saw Father get eaten by a whale!"

61
00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:35.228
As soon as Pinocchio said this, he started to cry.

62
00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:38.609
"Do not cry, Pinocchio.

63
00:03:39.249 --> 00:03:42.051
Your father is safe, but he is hidden.

64
00:03:43.111 --> 00:03:45.992
I will help you find him," said the Blue Fairy.

65
00:03:46.012 --> 00:03:48.073
"Father is alive?

66
00:03:48.793 --> 00:03:50.214
We should leave right now!"

67
00:03:50.674 --> 00:03:51.495
Pinocchio said.

68
00:03:51.515 --> 00:03:54.336
"No, Geppetto is safe.

69
00:03:55.276 --> 00:03:57.798
First, we must eat dinner and get some sleep.

70
00:03:58.538 --> 00:04:00.139
We will be stronger tomorrow."

71
00:04:00.159 --> 00:04:05.103
"I wish I were bigger and stronger," Pinocchio said.

72
00:04:05.123 --> 00:04:09.466
"If I were bigger and stronger, I could have saved Father.

73
00:04:10.166 --> 00:04:12.108
But, I'm only a piece of wood.

74
00:04:13.028 --> 00:04:16.310
I wish I were a real boy who could grow into a man."

75
00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:24.096
"Perhaps, if you are a good boy who obeys his father, you will become a real boy someday.

76
00:04:25.364 --> 00:04:27.589
But now, you must sleep, Pinocchio.

77
00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:30.475
We have a big day ahead of us tomorrow."
